 "observations": [
  "The page number «212» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the left the number of the table, «Tab. 97», in bold sans serif, underlined. The page has no signature and no title: the folios of the manuscripts stand at the left above the double rule of the first field, in one line of their own, «C 93v, O 149r–v, N 60r.», the letters raised, the short dash between r and v at their height (L01).",
  "The page holds three fields, as pp. 206-211 (JP2 0238-0243): «Quinque1) gradus Cancri» (L02), «Decem2) gradus Cancri» (L14) and «Quindecim3) gradus Cancri» (L22), the ascendant at 5°, 10° and 15° of Cancer, with the numbers for the sextile, the quadrature and the trine (L03, L15, L23); headings and numbers in bold. The columns begin with the sign of the ascendant: «Cancer Capricorn. Horoscopus4)», «Leo Aquarius Horoscopus», «Virgo Pisces Horoscopus», «Libra Aries Horoscopus», «Scorpius Taurus Horoscopus» and «Sagittar. Gemini Horoscopus4)», where C has «Matale» (note 4); here each head is set from the top, one printed line to a line (L04-L06), with «Gradus aequales», printed upwards, in L04-L05, and the units in L07. The numbers are counted from the beginning of Cancer: 5° 40′, 5° 33′ and 5° 40′ at 5° of Cancer, the oblique ascension of these 5° for the latitude 38° 30′ being 5° 33′ (computed with the obliquity 23° 35′). The second and the third field have no heads. Double rules divide the fields.",
  "The numbers at the head of a field, as on pp. 206-211 (JP2 0238-0243), are a third, a half and two thirds of one number. In the second field the sextile 61° 54′ and the quadrature 92° 50′ (L15) are a third and a half of the last number of the field, 185° 41′ (L21), the 92 the editor's for the 62 of all three manuscripts (note d); its two thirds are 123° 47.3′, where the trine has 124° 48′, the editor's 124 for the 120 of the manuscripts (note e), as if from 187° 12′. In the first field the sextile 61° 11′, the quadrature 91° 46′ and O's trine 122° 22′ (note a) are a third, a half and two thirds of 183° 33′, where the table has 180° 33′ at 30° of Sagittarius (L13; critical note); the edition's trine 122° 12′, from C, belongs to 183° 18′. In the third field the sextile 63° 53′ and the trine 127° 46′ (L23) are a third and two thirds of 191° 39′, and the quadrature 94° 50′ is half of 189° 40′, where the table has 189° 39′ (L29), whose third and two thirds are 63° 13′ and 126° 26′.",
  "The columns, as on pp. 208-211 (JP2 0240-0243): in Cancer and in Leo to its 20th degree the three fields lie within 14′, 24′ and 9′ of the oblique ascensions from the beginning of Cancer for the latitude 38° 30′ (computed with the obliquity 23° 35′); at 25° and 30° of Leo the first two fall 39′ to 45′ below them; from Virgo on all three fall far below them, to 180° 33′, 185° 41′ and 189° 39′ at the end of Sagittarius, where the oblique ascension from the beginning of Cancer is 220° 38′. At the end of Virgo (L13, L21, L29) each column stands 28′ to 37′ above the mean of its neighbours.",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked by the other fields, which differ by 5° of the ascendant, and by the steps of the columns: the edition's readings are the nearer in the quadrature of the second field (note d, L15: the editor's 92 for 62, above) and in the trine of the third (note f, L23: the 127 of O and N against C's 117(?), two thirds of 191° 39′ being 127° 46′). O's reading is the nearer in the trine of the first field (note a, L03: O's 122° 22′, two thirds of 183° 33′, against C's 122° 12′ and N's 123° 22′); the reading of O and N at 20° of Libra in the first field (note b, L11: their 38 against C's 28, the steps 4° 10′ and 4° 18′ against 4° 0′ and 4° 28′, the steps before and after being 4° 18′ and 4° 17′; the repetition of the field on p. 213, JP2 0245, L12, has 119° 38′); C's at 25° of Sagittarius in the first (note c, L12: with the last number 183° 33′, C's 178 gives the steps 5° 2′ and 5° 28′, as 5° 0′ and 5° 25′, 5° 10′ and 5° 25′ at the end of Sagittarius in the other fields, L20-L21, L28-L29, and O's 177, which the edition prints, 4° 2′ and 6° 28′; the repetition of the field on p. 213, JP2 0245, L13, has 178° 5′). The editor's 124 in the trine of the second field (note e) does not agree with the rule (above).",
  "The long dash before «Trigonum» in L23, and those before the notes b and f in N03 and N04, are each made up of two short dashes (15 and 19 px with a gap of 5 px; 14 and 16 px, 6 px; 22 and 14 px, 2 px; 36 to 39 px together); here written as two hyphens (U+2010). In N01 the note number 3 before «Quindecim» is printed on the line in the size of the text: see the critical note."
